import{_ as i,o as n,c as a,a2 as t}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 632 | Time Domain and Infinite Expansion | Scalability Argument of the Time-Domain System","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 632 | Time Domain and Infinite Expansion | Scalability Argument of the Time-Domain System","no":632,"module":3,"tags":["Infinite Expansion","Scalability","Time Domain","Multi-Plane","System Evolution"],"related":["80-Plane Theory and Classification","78-Cross-Plane Exploration Era","98-Extended-Setting Recommendation Checklist"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0632_模块3-时间域无限扩容-可扩展性论证.md","filePath":"en/0632_模块3-时间域无限扩容-可扩展性论证.md"}'),o={name:"en/0632_模块3-时间域无限扩容-可扩展性论证.md"};function s(l,e,r,d,c,h){return n(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[t('<h1 id="entry-632-time-domain-and-infinite-expansion-scalability-argument-of-the-time-domain-system" tabindex="-1">Entry 632 | Time Domain and Infinite Expansion | Scalability Argument of the Time-Domain System <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-632-time-domain-and-infinite-expansion-scalability-argument-of-the-time-domain-system" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 632 | Time Domain and Infinite Expansion | Scalability Argument of the Time-Domain System&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 3 · Dual-Track Time Domain | Benchmark base: Documents 80, 78, 98 | Series: Time Domain and Law-First Axiom (Entry 2)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-civilization-will-keep-merging-new-planes-—-can-the-time-domain-hold-up" tabindex="-1">Introduction: civilization will keep merging new planes — can the time domain hold up <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-civilization-will-keep-merging-new-planes-—-can-the-time-domain-hold-up" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: civilization will keep merging new planes — can the time domain hold up&quot;">​</a></h2><p>One of law-first axiom&#39;s promises is &quot;worldview may infinitely expand without collapse.&quot; For the dual-track time domain to live up to this promise, it must answer a forward-looking question: <strong>as civilization keeps merging new planes and接入 new Myriad Ranks, can the time-domain system still hold up?</strong> This entry argues the time-domain system&#39;s scalability — why it may expand from a small cosmos to cross-plane, hyper-multiverse, without collapsing.</p><p>Among the six top-level axioms, law-first axiom and republican axiom of Myriad Races are this entry&#39;s protagonists: scalability must be law-self-consistent (law-first), and must not leave any clan behind during expansion (Myriad-Race Republicanism); the other three — anti-predation, collective ascension, causal self-discipline — jointly constrain the expansion&#39;s way. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-three-layers-of-scalability" tabindex="-1">I. Three Layers of Scalability <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-three-layers-of-scalability" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Three Layers of Scalability&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The time-domain system&#39;s scalability divides into three progressive layers:</p><ol><li><strong>Intra-plane expansion</strong>: within an already merged plane, continuously add acceleration-domain/Quest-domain nodes, capacity, gears.</li><li><strong>Cross-plane expansion</strong>:接入 the time-domain interface to newly merged planes, letting new planes&#39; beings also use the dual track.</li><li><strong>Scale expansion</strong>: from material plane to energy layer, consciousness domain, law network; the time domain expands toward higher scales.</li></ol><p>Three layers, magnified level by level, but none starts over — this is scalability&#39;s essence.</p><h2 id="ii-why-it-can-expand-three-design-pivots" tabindex="-1">II. Why It Can Expand: Three Design Pivots <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-it-can-expand-three-design-pivots" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why It Can Expand: Three Design Pivots&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The time domain&#39;s scalability rests on three design pivots:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Pivot</th><th>Content</th><th>Expansion Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interface Standardization</td><td>Alaya Network access protocol (Entry 614), switching protocol (Entry 612) are both public standards</td><td>New planes接入 by standard, no custom development</td></tr><tr><td>Resource Incrementalization</td><td>Energy by incremental development (Entry 613), the more used the more</td><td>Expansion does not cut the stock cake</td></tr><tr><td>Algorithm Publication</td><td>Allocation, conversion, load models public</td><td>New clans apply by their own parameters</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Three pivots mean: <strong>expansion is &quot;access,&quot; not &quot;rebuild&quot;</strong>. This is scalability&#39;s engineering essence.</p><h2 id="iii-risks-and-hedging-in-expansion" tabindex="-1">III. Risks and Hedging in Expansion <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-risks-and-hedging-in-expansion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Risks and Hedging in Expansion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Expansion is not risk-free. Main risks and hedging:</p><ul><li><strong>Risk 1: heterogeneous planes&#39; time-unit differences</strong>. Newly merged planes&#39; time laws may differ from the origin plane. Hedge: time-unit conversion model (Entry 622) adapts by plane, does not assume unified time.</li><li><strong>Risk 2: expansion too fast causing causal overheating</strong>. Many new planes simultaneously接入, causal forks surge. Hedge: cross-plane exploration (Document 78) batches access, each batch does stress testing.</li><li><strong>Risk 3: new clans&#39; integration pain</strong>. Newly merged Myriad Ranks unfamiliar with dual-track rules. Hedge: the Quest Domain provides &quot;new-plane adaptation courses,&quot; helping them get familiar with rules.</li></ul><h2 id="iv-expansion-and-the-balanced-anchor-hyper-multiverse-realm-interface" tabindex="-1">IV. Expansion and the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm Interface <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-expansion-and-the-balanced-anchor-hyper-multiverse-realm-interface" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Expansion and the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm Interface&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The time domain&#39;s final expansion direction is serving civilization&#39;s move toward the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm (above Origin). Scalability argument therefore has long-term meaning:</p><ul><li>Only if the time-domain system may infinitely expand with civilization does civilization dare move toward cross-multiverse scale.</li><li>Each expansion makes the dual-track time domain&#39;s interfaces, algorithms, institutions one notch more mature.</li><li>The expansion process itself is the ongoing verification of law-first axiom&#39;s &quot;never collapse.&quot;</li></ul><p>In other words, <strong>scalability is not &quot;is it enough now,&quot; but &quot;will it still hold when infinitely expanded in the future&quot;</strong>.</p><h2 id="supplementary-argument-only-what-is-scalable-is-a-living-system" tabindex="-1">Supplementary Argument: Only What Is Scalable Is a Living System <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplementary-argument-only-what-is-scalable-is-a-living-system" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplementary Argument: Only What Is Scalable Is a Living System&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A system that can only serve one plane, one group of beings, no matter how exquisite, will eventually dry up with that plane&#39;s evolution. The dual-track time domain pursues scalability, essentially pursuing &quot;alive&quot; — it presets no endpoint, treats no plane as the last piece of the puzzle. Standardized interfaces let new planes plug-and-play; incremental energy makes it richer with expansion; public algorithms let clans apply as needed. This design philosophy contrasts with predatory-faction systems&#39; dead end of &quot;closed cosmos, expansion = collapse.&quot; Scalability is not a technical parameter, but a civilizational attitude: believing the future is bigger than the present, so every brick laid today must leave interfaces for tomorrow&#39;s building.</p><h2 id="brief-transition" tabindex="-1">Brief Transition <a class="header-anchor" href="#brief-transition" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Brief Transition&quot;">​</a></h2><p>When expanding, the Origin Acceleration Domain and Quest Sediment Domain must接入 new planes in pairs — cannot only give new planes the fast track without the slow track, otherwise newly merged beings repeat the old disease of acceleration emptying experience. The dual-track interface, Alaya Network access protocol, time-unit conversion model, as a complete standard open to new planes, ensuring the Origin Acceleration Domain and Quest Sediment Domain hold equally in new planes.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: interface standardization makes new-plane access zero redundant construction; expansion itself is efficiency</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: expansion relies on incremental resources and standard access, not annexing new planes&#39; stock</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo&#39;s system closed, expansion = collapse; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s time domain open, expansion = growth</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: during expansion, five lineages, newly merged clans all fairly接入 by conversion model</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: interfaces, algorithms, courses all public; any new plane may seamlessly接入 the dual track</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Whether a system is good does not only depend on how strong it is now, but on whether it can grow with civilization. The dual-track time domain, through three pivots of standardized interfaces, incremental resources, public algorithms, proves its own scalability — from one plane to countless, from material layer to law network; access rather than rebuild, expansion rather than collapse. This is law-first axiom&#39;s &quot;worldview may infinitely expand&quot; landing in the time dimension: <strong>the time-domain system, with civilization, moves toward the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm</strong>.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/80-位面理论与分类.html">Entry 80 · Plane Theory and Classification</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/78-跨位面探索纪元.html">Entry 78 · Cross-Plane Exploration Era</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/98-扩展设定建议清单.html">Entry 98 · Extended-Setting Recommendation Checklist</a> · <a href="./631_模块3-时间域法则优先-设定自洽性验证.html">Entry 631 · Self-Consistency Verification</a></li></ul>',30)])])}const u=i(o,[["render",s]]);export{p as __pageData,u as default};
